    "title": "Jacksonville-based UpShot League says it will start play with $40 million in investment - NewsBreak",
    "text": "7 hours ago The Jacksonville-based UpShot League of professional women’s basketball teams is set to begin play May 15 with $40 million in investments, the league said May 6. During a news conference, league co-founder Andy Kaufmann said the league had attracted 90 investors and financial partners for its inaugural season. Formation of the league was announced in January 2025 by Zawyer Sports & Entertainment, which owns, operates and manages the league. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
